    text: "PR #1479 current compensated-create/format-neutral diagnostic revision again reaches the unchanged 1200-second linked full-source deadline before final summary/next stage. No coverage-summary artifact exists. The output also retains a regression-child shutdown assertion at its original 5000ms bound; this is a recorded local runner qualification, not a diagnosis or current global pass. Focused SDK/CLI/MCP and format tests pass; exact final-head hosted coverage remains mandatory. Deadlines and coverage bounds remain unchanged."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T10:39:35.845Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "October 17 read-context delivery qualification: the unchanged CLI transport gate reports qualified product-budget failures on this host. Current isolated measurement exceeds next (459ms vs 440ms bound) and create (405ms vs 398ms); the original eeeaf3ececc4fc18c6c41cf3c4a5d3218e92a0aa revision, built separately with the same dependency graph, also fails create (399ms vs 398ms). Bare-Node controls remain qualified. These observations do not establish cause or certify a local latency pass; budgets are unchanged, and final-head hosted Gates (static) remains mandatory. Reuse this canonical investigation instead of creating another benchmark item."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T13:17:35.944Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR1490 review follow-up local transport-floor observation: qualified runner, context best434ms against433ms ceiling, p50=455ms, p95=490ms; all other operations pass. The earlier independently built original-base create399ms/398ms observation remains separate evidence. No causal equivalence or latency fix is claimed; existing budgets and admission rules remain unchanged. Current revised source must pass the hosted static gate before merge."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T17:08:50.326Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "October17 SDK-isolation local static run: unchanged CLI transport floor refuses with benchmark_product_budget_exceeded on a qualified Node26.9.0 runner. Best observations are get385ms/362ms, next456ms/440ms, create424ms/398ms and claim417ms/415ms; bare-Node controls remain qualified. The same gate, budgets, sample counts and admission policy are unchanged by this delivery. This is a current local refusal, not a diagnosis or latency pass; preserve the existing independently built baseline observations and require final-head hosted Gates(static) before merge. Other local static stages through tracker-quality and SDK-import checks pass."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T17:58:39.268Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR #1492 source head 14535f098 passes the unchanged hosted Gates (static), SDK import and CLI transport admission after the documented local qualified-budget refusals. CodSpeed also emits a +1.2 percent encodeQueryCursor comparison with a different-runtime-environments warning; pagination source and its benchmark are unchanged, so this is not attributed as a measured improvement caused by the isolation patch. No latency, RSS, sample, control-qualification or coverage threshold changed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T18:41:46.279Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Revised PR #1492 local static run passes every stage through SDK public-surface and ten entrypoint import-cost checks, then the unchanged qualified transport floor refuses claim: best 628ms versus 415ms; get/next/create pass this run. Node26 Linux control medians49/71ms remain within106ms runner qualification. Earlier source-head hosted static passed; final revised-head hosted static remains mandatory. No budget or runner qualification was weakened; causality is unproven. Metadata-only head098942 also has a CodSpeed cursor-decode comparison warning across different runtime environments; cursor source and benchmark were unchanged, so retain that comparison as qualified evidence rather than a demonstrated source regression."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T21:24:53.429Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Fresh read-only validation observation: the qualified Node26.9.0 SDK import-cost gate rejects ./sdk/graph at median232ms against172ms; before/after control medians52ms/49ms remain within106ms. This is a product-admission failure, not an unqualified-runner result. No budget, denominator, or control policy was changed, and no startup optimization is claimed. The reviewed hosted Node24 admission remains required on the final head. Keep this observation separate from prior transport-floor reports."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T21:34:00.014Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Follow-up qualification evidence, without changing code or thresholds: one standalone full-entrypoint admission still rejects qualified Node26 (graph181ms>172ms and several wider entrypoints); a subsequent paired five-sample graph comparison built the unchanged main base9baac800 in an external tracker-isolated archive and alternated baseline/candidate imports. Base median161ms, candidate156ms, bare controls65ms/69ms. This does not reproduce a graph import regression in this patch and does not erase either failed admission cohort. CLI transport-floor admission also remains failed under its existing budgets; retain the broader qualification/startup work as open."
  - created_at: "2026-10-17T23:02:32.103Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The later complete pnpm quality:static run on the history revision passed all gates, including the unchanged SDK-entrypoint and CLI-transport-floor admissions. Preserve the earlier qualified Node26 failures and paired-main comparison as historical observations; this passing cohort does not establish that every host or runtime distribution meets its budgets. No qualification rule or threshold was relaxed."
